{
  "card": "Shadow Urchin",
  "title": "the \"creature you control with counters dies\" trigger has an unknown mode and never fires",
  "status": "active",
  "kind": "parser",
  "upstream_issue": null,
  "marks_supported": true,
  "applies_to": {
    "server_version": "0.117.0",
    "build_commit": "09c286c",
    "card_data_sha256": "84d5fd2af84e2f125b740eeb05637785b2e8df26d34e41a2cd628697dae30513",
    "entry_sha256": "b8ce70c0170d2c42782c32847fe475d9c3f8b65b8395a366eb7ccf109188df40"
  },
  "rules": {
    "oracle": "Whenever this creature attacks, blight 1. (Put a -1/-1 counter on a creature you control.)\nWhenever a creature you control with one or more counters on it dies, exile that many cards from the top of your library. Until your next end step, you may play those cards.",
    "cr": [
      "603.2",
      "603.6c",
      "603.10a",
      "700.4",
      "608.2h",
      "122.2",
      "611.2a"
    ],
    "actual": "The second trigger has `mode: Unknown(\"Whenever a creature you control with one or more counters on it dies\")` with no `valid_card`, so it never triggers: nothing is exiled when a creature you control dies with counters on it.",
    "expected": "Whenever a creature you control dies (battlefield to graveyard, CR 700.4) and it had one or more counters on it as it last existed on the battlefield (CR 603.10a, 608.2h), you exile that many cards from the top of your library, counting every counter of every kind, and you may play them until your next end step. It sees Shadow Urchin's own death too (a leaves-the-battlefield trigger looks back in time, CR 603.10a). A creature without counters, or an opponent's creature, does nothing.",
    "diagnosis": "The trigger-subject parser recognizes \"Whenever a creature you control dies\" and \"Whenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it dies\", but not the counter-agnostic \"with one or more counters on it\" qualifier, so the whole trigger line falls through to `TriggerMode::Unknown`. The body was parsed (ExileTop plus the PlayFromExile permission until your next end step), but \"that many\" was left as `EventContextAmount`, which has no amount on a zone-change event.",
    "suggested_fix": "In the trigger parser, accept \"a creature you control with one or more counters on it dies\" (and \"with a counter on it\") as `TriggerMode::ChangesZone { origin: Battlefield, destination: Graveyard }` with `valid_card: Typed Creature controller You` and the condition `TriggerCondition::HadCounters { counter_type: None }`, which reads the departure LKI (game/triggers.rs:16419), the shape Felisa, Fang of Silverquill already gets for \"if it had counters on it\". Bind \"that many\" in the body to `QuantityRef::CountersOn { scope: EventSource }` (no counter type: all counters), again as for Felisa. Integration test: a creature with two +1/+1 counters dies and the top two cards are exiled and playable; a creature without counters dies and nothing happens.",
    "override_note": "The patch gives the trigger Felisa's tested shape: a ChangesZone battlefield-to-graveyard trigger (\"dies\", CR 700.4) for creatures you control, gated on HadCounters with no counter type, which reads the creature's counters from its last-known information as it left the battlefield (CR 603.10a, 608.2h; counters cease to exist on a zone change, CR 122.2), and \"that many\" is the number of counters of all kinds on it then (CountersOn EventSource). As a leaves-the-battlefield trigger it also sees Shadow Urchin's own death (CR 603.10a). A gate on the dying creature's state as it left is the same as the trigger event's \"with one or more counters on it\": it is checked on that last-known information both when the trigger event happens and, being unchanging, on resolution. The exile and the play permission until your next end step (upstream's existing ExileTop and PlayFromExile with UntilNextStepOf End) are unchanged. In the sandbox with the override, exiled cards were also actually cast in the windows the cases show as offered."
  },
  "patch": [
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/triggers/1/mode",
      "value": {
        "Unknown": "Whenever a creature you control with one or more counters on it dies"
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/triggers/1/valid_card",
      "value": null
    },
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/triggers/1/condition",
      "value": null
    },
    {
      "op": "test",
      "path": "/triggers/1/execute/effect/count",
      "value": {
        "type": "Ref",
        "qty": {
          "type": "EventContextAmount"
        }
      }
    },
